:name: HWA10-trace
:description: Capture a boot PC trace for the coverage progress bar (coverage.py).
# Native Renode ExecutionTracer (fast) — NOT per-instruction Python hooks.
# Only lightweight hooks: sd_mbr_command patch + log-ring unblock so boot reaches
# the scheduler. No uart file backend, no putchar hook (those slow tracing).
# After running:  python3 coverage.py out/trace.bin.gz

using sysbus
mach create "hwa10"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @hwa10.repl
sysbus ApplySVD @NRF52840.svd
sysbus LoadBinary @flash.bin 0x0
cpu VectorTableOffset 0x0
cpu PerformanceInMips 300

sysbus WriteWord 0x9301e 0x2000
cpu AddHook 0x3b4c0 """
if cpu.GetRegisterUnsafe(0).RawValue==0xb2588:
    b=cpu.GetMachine().SystemBus
    b.WriteDoubleWord(b.ReadDoubleWord(0xb2588)+0x11c, 1)
"""
cpu AddHook 0x3b444 """
if cpu.GetRegisterUnsafe(0).RawValue==0xb2588:
    b=cpu.GetMachine().SystemBus
    b.WriteDoubleWord(b.ReadDoubleWord(0xb2588)+0x11c, 1)
"""

cpu CreateExecutionTracing "tr" @/tmp/hwa10_trace.bin.gz PC isBinary=True compress=True
emulation RunFor "0.35"
cpu DisableExecutionTracing
quit
